- spellings:
  - --x86-align-branch
  value_name: <string>
  value_kind: Required
  choices:
  - name: jcc
    description: indicates conditional jumps
  - name: fused
    description: indicates fused conditional jumps
  - name: jmp
    description: indicates direct unconditional jumps
  - name: call
    description: indicates direct and indirect calls
  - name: ret
    description: indicates rets
  group: 'General options:'
  description: 'Specify types of branches to align (plus separated list of types): indirect indicates indirect unconditional jumps'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --x86-align-branch-boundary
  value_name: <uint>
  value_kind: Required
  group: 'General options:'
  description: Control how the assembler should align branches with NOP. If the boundary's size is not 0, it should be a power of 2 and no less than 32. Branches will be aligned to prevent from being across or against the boundary of specified size. The default value 0 does not align branches.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --x86-branches-within-32B-boundaries
  group: 'General options:'
  description: Align selected instructions to mitigate negative performance impact of Intel's micro code update for errata skx102. May break assumptions about labels corresponding to particular instructions, and should be used with caution.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --x86-pad-max-prefix-size
  value_name: <uint>
  value_kind: Required
  group: 'General options:'
  description: Maximum number of prefixes to use for padding
  provenance:
    sources:
